---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import '../styles/prose.css';

const description =
  'Three on-ramps into the Retro-Active ecosystem: discrete-logic builder, FPGA builder, software developer.';
---

<PageLayout title="Getting Started" description={description}>
  <div class="intro">
    <h1>Getting Started</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Pick the path that matches your background. Every path loops back to the
      others &mdash; you don&rsquo;t have to commit to one.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="path-grid">
    <section class="path-card" aria-labelledby="path-discrete">
      <p class="path-kicker" aria-hidden="true">// path_01</p>
      <h2 id="path-discrete">I want to build with discrete logic</h2>
      <p class="path-audience">For the 74-series, PAL/GAL, and breadboard crowd &mdash; no FPGA required.</p>
      <ol class="path-steps">
        <li>
          Read the <a href="/learn-fpga/architecture/">Architecture</a> page
          to learn the common bus signals, timing, and memory map.
        </li>
        <li>
          Pick a CPU family you want to build around. The classics &mdash;
          6502, Z80, 6809, 68000, 8088 &mdash; all map cleanly onto the bus.
        </li>
        <li>
          Prototype on a breadboard or perfboard. Start with CPU, RAM, and a
          simple output (LEDs or UART) before adding cards.
        </li>
        <li>
          Design your first card &mdash; address decoder, UART, or a simple
          peripheral. Plain 74-logic or a PAL/GAL for decode works fine.
        </li>
        <li>
          Share schematics, BOMs, and timing notes back to the community so
          others can build compatible cards.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="path-card" aria-labelledby="path-fpga">
      <p class="path-kicker" aria-hidden="true">// path_02</p>
      <h2 id="path-fpga">I want to build with an FPGA</h2>
      <p class="path-audience">For builders who want to pack a lot onto one board with open-source tools.</p>
      <ol class="path-steps">
        <li>
          Install the open-source FPGA toolchain: Yosys, nextpnr, and
          OpenFPGALoader. Start at
          <a href="https://yosyshq.net/" rel="noopener">yosyshq.net</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Get an affordable starter board. Suggested: Colorlight i5 (ECP5)
          or an ICE40-based board. See the
          <a href="/learn-fpga/projects/">Projects</a> page.
        </li>
        <li>
          Read the <a href="/learn-fpga/architecture/">Architecture</a> page
          so your soft-core or peripheral can talk the common bus.
        </li>
        <li>
          Clone the reference implementation at
          <a href="https://github.com/benpayne/learn-fpga" rel="noopener">github.com/benpayne/learn-fpga</a>
          and synthesize a known-good config.
        </li>
        <li>
          Start modifying: drop in your own CPU, add a peripheral card,
          share the bitstream and RTL back to the community.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="path-card" aria-labelledby="path-software">
      <p class="path-kicker" aria-hidden="true">// path_03</p>
      <h2 id="path-software">I want to write software</h2>
      <p class="path-audience">For C/C++ developers new to embedded or bare-metal work.</p>
      <ol class="path-steps">
        <li>
          Install the GCC retro back-end for your target CPU family
          (6502, Z80, 68k, 8086, or RISC-V). GCC and its ports cover most
          of the classic ISAs.
        </li>
        <li>
          Read <a href="/learn-fpga/blog/">Portable Drivers with GCC</a> to
          understand how one driver can target many systems that speak the
          common bus.
        </li>
        <li>
          Pick a reference build (or your own) and get a &ldquo;hello world&rdquo;
          running over UART. This is the loop you&rsquo;ll iterate in.
        </li>
        <li>
          Write a driver for a peripheral card you care about. Contribute
          it back so every system that has that card gets it for free.
        </li>
        <li>
          Port a retro app: try recompiling a FreeDOS or EmuTOS utility
          for <em>your</em> system.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="closing" aria-labelledby="closing-heading">
    <h2 id="closing-heading">Every Path Leads Home</h2>
    <p>
      All three audiences benefit from the same shared work. A card designed
      with plain 74-logic and a card synthesized into an FPGA can look
      identical to the software above them. A driver written for one system
      works on every other system that speaks the bus. Blog posts written
      for beginners save experts time. Pick a starting point, follow your
      thread, and when you look up you&rsquo;ll find you&rsquo;ve been
      building on everyone else&rsquo;s work &mdash; and they&rsquo;re
      building on yours.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="next" aria-labelledby="next-heading">
    <p class="next-kicker" aria-hidden="true">// next</p>
    <h2 id="next-heading">Where to go next</h2>
    <ul class="next-links">
      <li><a href="/learn-fpga/blog/">Blog &rarr; deep dives and build logs</a></li>
      <li><a href="/learn-fpga/architecture/">Architecture &rarr; the common bus standard</a></li>
      <li><a href="/learn-fpga/projects/">Projects &rarr; community showcase</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .intro {
    max-width: var(--max-prose);
    margin-inline: auto;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-48);
  }

  .intro h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-16);
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ---------- Three-path grid ---------- */

  .path-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-24);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-64);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .path-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .path-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      gap: var(--space-32);
    }
  }

  /* ---------- Path card ---------- */

  .path-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-accent) 2%, var(--color-bg));
    padding: var(--space-24);
    border-radius: 2px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .path-card:hover {
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-accent) 40%, var(--color-border));
  }

  .path-kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--color-accent-alt);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-8) 0;
  }

  .path-card h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-8) 0;
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .path-card h2 {
      font-size: 1.35rem;
    }
  }

  .path-audience {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-16) 0;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .path-steps {
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: step;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-12);
  }

  .path-steps li {
    counter-increment: step;
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 2.25rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
  }

  .path-steps li::before {
    content: counter(step, decimal-leading-zero);
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-accent-alt);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .path-steps code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85em;
    color: var(--color-accent-alt);
    background-color: rgba(255, 176, 0, 0.08);
    padding: 0.05em 0.3em;
    border-radius: 3px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .path-steps a {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--color-border);
    text-underline-offset: 0.15em;
  }

  .path-steps a:hover,
  .path-steps a:focus {
    text-decoration-color: var(--color-accent-alt);
  }

  /* ---------- Closing section ---------- */

  .closing {
    max-width: var(--max-prose);
    margin-inline: auto;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-48);
    padding-block: var(--space-24);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .closing h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-16) 0;
  }

  .closing p {
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ---------- Next section ---------- */

  .next {
    max-width: var(--max-prose);
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .next-kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-8) 0;
  }

  .next h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-16) 0;
  }

  .next-links {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .next-links a {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1rem;
    display: inline-block;
    padding: var(--space-8) 0;
  }
</style>
